# Tuto Web Dashboard — Product Requirements Document (PRD v1)

**Audience:** Cursor acting as a *senior* full‑stack engineer (web) and release captain.
**Scope:** A new **web dashboard/website** for Tuto Schools (school admins & teachers) and Tuto Ops (platform admins), built alongside the existing mobile app.
**Non‑negotiable constraint:** **Do not modify** the **mobile app** code (apps/mobile) while working on web. Shared packages may be added/updated *without breaking mobile* (see Guardrails).
**Always read this file whenever continuing for the web version**
---
Create new files,
1. web version progress tracker - update this file after every session to update the progress by date, don't delete anything in this file but add for the next session in a seperate entry by date
2. new chat summary file for the web version to have clear and detailed information on the session for the new chat window
3. features checklist file - use this file to keep and update on the features that are listed below and which have been implemented and update for any challenges and tasks which need my involvement

## 1) Problem & Goals

### 1.1 What are we solving?

School admins need a browser‑based control center to manage teachers, students, classes, bookings, payments, and reporting. Tuto Ops needs moderation, approvals, and platform analytics. Parents may optionally get read‑only access later.

### 1.2 Why now?

Mobile is not efficient for back‑office workflows, bulk operations, or analysis. Web unlocks productivity (tables, exports), oversight (dashboards), and compliance (audit, data retention) needed for production readiness and monetization.

### 1.3 Primary goals (P0)

* **Secure, role‑aware** web portal for School Admins and Tuto Admins.
* Daily operations: **Teachers, Classes, Students, Bookings, Payments** (read → manage).
* **Reporting** starter dashboards for core KPIs.
* **Moderation** starter for reviews/UGC.
* Ship with **Sentry**, **analytics**, **CI**, and strict **API security**.

### 1.4 Non‑goals (for v1)

* Parent self‑service portal (P2).
* Deep LMS authoring (basic assignments only in P1).
* Replatforming the backend away from Airtable (future).

---

## 2) Users & Roles

* **Tuto Admin** (platform‑wide ops): approvals, moderation, global payments/analytics.
* **School Admin** (tenant): manages the school, teachers, classes, students, bookings, invoices.
* **Teacher** (tenant staff): limited access to own classes/students (read, attendance, assignments).
* **Parent** (optional P2): read‑only student schedule, payments, progress.

> Authorization derives from Firebase Auth custom claims `{ role, schoolIds[] }`.

---

## 3) Success Metrics

* Admin time to perform common tasks (target −50%).
* Booking pipeline visibility (all states visible, actionable).
* Crash‑free sessions ≥ 99.5%, P95 page load < 2.5s.
* Security: no public generic CRUD, strict CORS, server validation for writes.

---

## 4) Product Surface (Information Architecture)

### 4.1 Global

* **/login**, **/logout**, **/onboarding**
* **/** (role‑aware landing)
* **/settings** (profile, school/org settings, billing, legal)
* **/help** (FAQ/docs links)

### 4.2 School Admin workspace

* **/schools/[id]/overview** — KPIs: active students, classes this week, revenue MTD, pending invoices, churn risk.
* **/schools/[id]/teachers** — list, filter, create/edit, verification status, availability, ratings.
* **/schools/[id]/students** — CRM: profiles, contacts, enrollment, progress flags, fees status.
* **/schools/[id]/classes** — courses, schedules, capacity, roster, attendance.
* **/schools/[id]/bookings** — pipeline view (pending/confirmed/cancelled/no‑show), actions.
* **/schools/[id]/payments** — invoices/receipts, payouts, refunds, reconciliation.
* **/schools/[id]/lms** — basic assignments to class/student, results roll‑up.
* **/schools/[id]/reviews** — ratings, comments, replies, hide/show.
* **/schools/[id]/reports** — exports (CSV/PDF) for teachers, students, bookings, revenue.

### 4.3 Tuto Admin workspace

* **/admin/approvals** — teacher/school approvals.
* **/admin/moderation** — UGC triage (posts, comments, reviews, reports, blocks).
* **/admin/payments** — platform‑level reconciliation, refund policies.
* **/admin/analytics** — marketplace KPIs by city/subject.
* **/admin/schemas** — read‑only schema v1 doc & migrations.

---

## 5) Functional Requirements (WHAT & brief HOW)

> **API rule:** All web calls go through **Firebase Functions /v1** (no direct Airtable from client). Requests include **Firebase ID token**; server enforces **role + schoolId** authorization and **Zod** validation.

### 5.1 Auth & Tenancy (P0)

**What:** Web login via Firebase Auth; role‑aware navigation; school context switcher.
**Why:** Single identity with mobile, least friction; secure multi‑tenant access.
**How (brief):** Next.js client uses Firebase Auth; on login, fetch claims; store school context in URL or provider; protect routes (HOC/middleware) and menu by role.
**DoD:** Unauthed users cannot access protected pages; wrong role/tenant can’t see or call restricted endpoints.

### 5.2 Teachers (P0)

**What:** List, filter/sort, create/edit teacher; view verification, ratings, availability.
**Why:** School ops require quick teacher management.
**How:** Data table with pagination; drawer for create/edit; optimistic updates reconcile with server truth.
**DoD:** CRUD works with validation; list states (loading/empty/error) present; audit log entries appear for writes.

### 5.3 Students (P0)

**What:** List + profile; enrollment, contact info, fees status; CSV export.
**Why:** CRM basics for schools.
**How:** Data table + profile page; server validation; export button calling a report endpoint.
**DoD:** Accurate filtering/export; no PII leaks in client logs.

### 5.4 Classes (P0)

**What:** Create/edit class; schedule, capacity; roster & attendance.
**Why:** Operational heart of teaching.
**How:** Form with validation; schedule visual; roster tab; attendance toggles.
**DoD:** Class shows in schedules; attendance persisted; constraints enforced server‑side.

### 5.5 Bookings (P0)

**What:** Pipeline across states (pending/confirmed/cancelled/no‑show) with actions.
**Why:** Visibility and fast resolution drive revenue.
**How:** Kanban/table hybrid; action drawers (confirm/cancel/no‑show); optimistic + reconcile.
**DoD:** State changes audit‑logged; totals match reports; no phantom states.

### 5.6 Payments (P0)

**What:** List invoices/receipts; basic reconciliation view.
**Why:** Financial clarity & support.
**How:** Read‑first; later actions in P1; webhook data reflected in UI.
**DoD:** Records match gateway events; mismatches flagged.

### 5.7 Reviews & Moderation (P0)

**What:** List reviews; approve/hide; see reports.
**Why:** Trust & safety.
**How:** Table with bulk actions; role‑gated.
**DoD:** Actions reflected immediately; audit present; non‑admins cannot access.

### 5.8 Reporting (P0)

**What:** Overview dashboard (KPIs) + CSV exports.
**Why:** Operability and insight.
**How:** Recharts for KPIs; export endpoints for CSV.
**DoD:** KPIs accurate for selected time range; exports open in Excel.

### 5.9 LMS Basics (P1)

**What:** Assign exercises to class/student; track completion.
**Why:** Learning outcomes and retention.
**How:** Assignment templates, assign modal, results tab.
**DoD:** Assignment → completion visible on student profile and class view.

### 5.10 Refunds & Reconciliation (P1)

**What:** Issue refunds; reconcile discrepancies; receipts/ledger reflect status.
**Why:** Support and finance hygiene.
**How:** Refund action (role‑gated), webhook confirmation, idempotent handlers.
**DoD:** Refunds appear in ledger; bookings updated; audit present.

### 5.11 Advanced Moderation (P1)

**What:** UGC triage queue, severity filters, batch actions.
**Why:** Scale trust & safety.
**How:** Queue page; actions logged; rate‑limits enforced server‑side.
**DoD:** SLAs met; repeat abusers blocked; false positives minimized.

### 5.12 Analytics Dashboards (P1)

**What:** Funnels (search → booking) and retention; segment by city/subject.
**Why:** Marketplace health.
**How:** Embedded charts; shared taxonomy with mobile.
**DoD:** Dashboards match event data; deltas explained.

---

## 6) Architecture & Repo Strategy

* **Monorepo** (Workspaces): keep web and mobile together but isolated.

```
/apps
  /mobile        # existing mobile app (DO NOT MODIFY)
  /dashboard     # NEW Next.js app (web)
/packages
  /ui            # shared theme/components (non‑breaking for mobile)
  /schemas       # Zod schemas shared across apps & functions
  /api           # typed SDK for /v1 endpoints + React Query hooks
  /config        # shared eslint/tsconfig/tailwind
/functions       # Firebase Functions (secure /v1)
/docs            # schema.md v1, release, analytics, privacy, etc.
```

* **Backend contract**: Introduce **/v1** endpoints with auth, role checks, Zod validation, strict CORS, rate limiting, and audit logs. Deprecate old generic CRUD.
* **Data**: Airtable remains source of truth in v1; no client secrets.

---

## 7) Security & Compliance Requirements (hard)

* No public generic CRUD; only specific **/v1** endpoints.
* Every write validated (Zod) and **audit‑logged**.
* **Strict CORS** allowlist (dashboard + admin origins only).
* **Rate limiting** per UID/IP on sensitive endpoints.
* **Sentry** enabled with source maps; no PII in breadcrumbs.
* **Legal**: ToS/Privacy accessible; acceptance logged; age gate & consent flows (when applicable).

---

## 8) UX/UI Requirements (modern, smooth)

* **Design language**: minimal, airy, **rounded‑2xl**, consistent spacing scale, subtle shadows.
* **Components**: shadcn/ui primitives; DataTable with column visibility, sticky header, virtualization for large lists.
* **Icons**: lucide‑react; use meaningful affordances.
* **Animations**: **Framer Motion** for page transitions, drawers, toasts, skeleton fades. Keep durations short (120–240ms), easeOut.
* **States**: Every data surface has **loading** (skeletons), **empty** (illustration + helpful copy), **error** (actionable).
* **A11y**: keyboard focus rings, ARIA for tables/forms; high‑contrast mode acceptable.
* **Performance budgets**: First content < 2.5s (p95); smooth scroll on low‑end laptops; images sized responsively.
* **i18n**: EN/VI parity; numbers, currency (VND), distances localized.

---

## 9) Delivery Plan & Milestones

### Milestone P0 (4–6 sprints)

1. **Scaffold**: apps/dashboard, shared packages, auth shell, protected routes, design tokens.
2. **API contract**: /v1 endpoints for teachers, students, classes, bookings (read/write), payments (read), reviews (read+moderation), with auth/Zod/CORS/rate limit/audit.
3. **School Admin core**: Teachers, Classes, Students, Bookings (full CRUD/flows), Payments (read), Reviews (moderation lite), Overview KPIs, CSV exports.
4. **Ops**: Approvals & Moderation starter.
5. **Observability**: Sentry + analytics taxonomy; CI (lint/type/test/build) + Vercel previews.

**Exit criteria P0**: Guardrails met (Security & Compliance), no unauth routes, no crashes, core flows usable end‑to‑end.

### Milestone P1

* LMS basics (assignments → results), Refunds & reconciliation actions, Advanced moderation, Analytics dashboards.

### Milestone P2

* Parent portal (read‑only), timetable planner, email automations, white‑label theming.

---

## 10) Guardrails for Cursor (operate like a senior engineer)

* **Do not modify** mobile app code. If a *shared package* change is needed, ensure **no breaking changes** and run a mobile smoke build locally; if risky, fork a new shared component variant.
* **Small, cohesive PRs**: one feature or endpoint slice at a time, with tests and docs.
* **Branch naming**: `feat/<area>/<slug>`, `fix/<area>/<slug>`; Conventional Commits.
* **Quality gates per PR**:

  * Typecheck (tsc), ESLint/Prettier clean.
  * Unit tests and at least one smoke test for changed flows.
  * Sentry symbolication in preview build.
  * i18n strings extracted; VI/EN verified.
  * No client secrets; environment variables documented.
* **Safety first**: If a step would break mobile or production data, stop, mark **BLOCKED**, and continue with the next task.
* **Docs**: Update `/docs/schema.md` (if payloads change), `/docs/release.md`, `/docs/analytics.md`.
* **Non‑interactive execution**: Proceed through backlog without asking for confirmations; summarize at the end (Done/Blocked with reasons).

---

## 11) Acceptance Criteria (cross‑cutting)

* All protected pages require auth; unauthorized/forbidden states render friendly screens.
* Each list supports loading/empty/error/pagination; back/forward navigation preserves filters.
* Writes are validated and audit‑logged; errors actionable.
* Sentry shows symbolicated traces; analytics events align with taxonomy.
* Dashboard UI is modern, smooth, accessible, and consistent with mobile brand.

---

## 12) Risks & Mitigations

* **Backend gaps** (generic CRUD, lax CORS): address before enabling writes from web.
* **Tenant leaks**: enforce schoolId checks on every call; include unit tests for authorization.
* **Performance**: use virtualization for large tables; cache and paginate; image constraints.
* **Schema drift**: publish `docs/schema.md` v1 and gate changes via PR review.

---

## 13) Out of Scope (v1)

* Real‑time collaborative editing.
* External SSO for schools (consider later).
* Deep LMS authoring tools.

---

## 14) Handoff Notes

* Start in **monorepo** with `/apps/dashboard` and shared packages.
* Introduce `/v1` endpoints in Functions first; deprecate legacy routes with headers.
* Keep a running `PROGRESS.md` with links to PRs and notable decisions.
* Produce a brief end‑of‑sprint demo checklist and screenshots.
